            <ArticleTitle>Sirolimus-eluting stent thrombosis several years after clopidogrel discontinuation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E265-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Despite recent meta-analyses showing either similar rates or only slightly increased rates of stent thrombosis in patients with a drug-eluting stent, clinicians remain concerned about the risk of late stent thrombosis in these patients. We are reporting on a &quot;very-very&quot; late stent thrombosis that occurred 43 months post-implantation. We believe this represents the most delayed reported thrombosis post-sirolimus-eluting stent implantation, which might not have been preventable using even the latest FDA recommendations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
